[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Fourth Reference Slice - Nonlinear Diode Operating Points

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Iterations 151-200 introduce a bounded Shockley diode and analytic damped Newton DC operating points. This slice does not qualify semiconductor model parity, nonlinear transient integration, AC bias linearization, model plugins, or production convergence guarantees.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-001
TITLE: Validated diode model and conventions
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall represent a two-terminal Shockley diode with positive finite saturation current and thermal voltage, with terminal current defined from p to n.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/circuit.rs, src/model.rs.
Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::shockley_diode_has_positive_incremental_conductance, tests/nonlinear.rs::diode_circuit_parameters_are_validated_at_the_public_boundary.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-MOD-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-002
TITLE: Analytic bounded Newton operating point
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall solve diode operating points using an analytic residual and Jacobian, bounded line-search damping, finite trial checks and explicit iteration/tolerance limits.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/newton.rs, src/dc.rs.
Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::forward_biased_resistor_diode_bias_point_converges, tests/nonlinear.rs::high_bias_diode_uses_bounded_damping_instead_of_exponential_overflow, tests/nonlinear.rs::Newton_iteration_budget_is_a_real_failure_boundary.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-EQ-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-003
TITLE: Explicit nonlinear analysis boundaries
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall reject nonlinear AC and transient requests until bias linearization and per-step nonlinear integration are implemented, and expose Newton evidence in operating-point results.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/ac.rs, src/transient.rs, src/configured.rs, src/api.rs.
Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::nonlinear_ac_is_explicitly_unsupported_until_bias_linearization_exists, tests/nonlinear.rs::nonlinear_transient_is_rejected_until_newton_time_stepping_exists.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-004
TITLE: Typed nonlinear authoring and evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
The experimental JSON and C# authoring surfaces shall serialize diode and bounded Newton operating-point options, and successful nonlinear DC result manifests shall retain Newton convergence evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/api.rs, dotnet/Simulator.Client/Requests.cs, Results.cs.
Verification: dotnet/Simulator.Conformance/MoreChecks.cs, tests/nonlinear.rs::json_operating_point_manifest_exposes_newton_report_for_diode_case.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-005
TITLE: Reproducible continuation handoff
STATEMENT: >>>
The repository shall retain a top-level continuation prompt identifying the implemented nonlinear scope, intentional limitations, validation commands, and the next bounded engineering milestones.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: prompt.md.
Verification: prompt.md is reviewed at each final iteration checkpoint.
<<<
